{"type": "message", "message": "**Minimalist means less visual clutter—not less comfort or an empty home.** In a small flat, it usually means:\n\n- **Purposeful furniture:** enough for daily life, without lots of little extra pieces.\n- **Clear routes:** arrange furniture so doors, windows and walking paths stay accessible.\n- **A restrained palette:** a few repeating colours and materials, rather than everything matching.\n- **Useful storage:** closed cupboards keep everyday belongings handy but out of sight.\n- **Warmth through texture:** wood, woven fabrics and a rug can feel welcoming without looking busy.\n\nFor your combined living-and-dining room, that could mean two clearly defined zones with coordinated furniture—not stripping the room down to a sofa alone. Your existing warm off-white walls could be a good starting point.", "conversationId": "938bf777f8374b13996c5caa3a4bcec9"}
